ter 1120</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">7170</idno></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work3755"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">abhidharmasamuccaya</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos mngon pa kun las btus pa</title><author ref="person:3756">asaṅga</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">On Tibetan transmission lineages, see [TZC3JQWE].</note><idno type="APIS">3755</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5264"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos mngon kun las btus pa'i tikka</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཆོས་མངོན་ཀུན་ལས་བཏུས་པའི་ཏིཀཀ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mngon pa kun las btus pa'i Tik+ka</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mdo kun las btus pa'i TIk+ka</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1100-01-01" notAfter="1200-12-31">after 1100 before 1200</date><author ref="person:7170">Anonymous</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">The work contains a lineage of the Abhidharmasamuccaya (ID:3755) ending with Brang (ID:4291) and Ko (ID:4241). Its author was thus probably writing in the (early) 12th century.&#13;
